description.content:
Initiates or continues a conversation with the conversation exchange service.
The conversation exchange request and response cycle has the following steps.

1. Open a connection.

The conversation exchange service uses the secure WebSocket protocol (wss) at the following endpoint:
wss://{hostname}/api/conversation/v1/exchange/wss

After the connection is established, the client defines the event listeners (onOpen, onMessage, onClose, etc) to respond to events from the server.

2. Initiate an exchange request.

To initiate an exchange request, the client sends a JSON text message to the service over the established connection.
The client must send this message before it sends any audio.
The JSON text message must include an "action" parameter.

For example,
{
  "action": "START",
  "exchange_request": {
    "conversation_id": "conversation-59410397-aaa9-42f0-91ef-1e39f710edec",
    "input": {
      "option": {
        "audio_output_disabled": true,
      },
      "raw_audio": {
        "audio_encoding": "LINEAR16",
        "sample_rate_hertz": 16000,
      }
    }
  }
}

If the service receives the request successfully, the service returns the following JSON text message to indicate that it is "PROCESSING".

{
 "data": {
   "state": "PROCESSING"
 }
}

3. Send audio.

After the client sends the initial "START" message, it can start sending audio data to the service.
The client does not need to wait for the service to respond to the "START" message with the "PROCESSING" message.

4. End a request.

When the client is done sending the audio data, it must signal the service by sending a JSON text message with the action parameter set to the value of "STOP".

{
  "action": "STOP"
}

5. Receive exchange result

Once the service receives the "STOP" action from the client and finishes processing the request,
it will send a response JSON text message (CreateWsExchangeResponse message type) asynchronously,
followed by { "data": { "state" : "PROCESSING_COMPLETED" } } indicating that it's done sending the response.

